  "content": "<ul>\n\t\t\t<i></i>\n\t\t\t<i></i>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t<li>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.metabunk.org/threads/what-is-this-white-water-can-it-tied-back-to-nimitz-tic-tac-encounter.15135/post-377384\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t#1\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t</ul>\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<p>The white water has always been one of the most unexplained aspects of the Nimitz UFO encounter to me. I thought it best to discuss it separately and consider any possible connection to the Nimitz Tic Tac encounter and its location.</p><p>\n\n\nA recent <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/whatisit/comments/1x5tl84/i_was_flying_a_drone_at_work_and_this_white_thing/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Reddit video</a> shows a sudden white disturbance. the OP states the location off Rivière-au-Renard, Gaspésie, Quebec. </p><p><img src=\"https://www.metabunk.org/attachments/1792038857747-png.93640/\" alt=\"1792038857747.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"724\" height=\"223\" />\n\t</p><p>\naround 400m of the coast,</p><p><img src=\"https://www.metabunk.org/attachments/1792038964380-png.93641/\" alt=\"1792038964380.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"734\" height=\"237\" />\n\t</p><p>\nThe OP reported shallow water, about 5ft deep , it exploded suddenly, spread of roughly 300 metres,</p><p><img src=\"https://www.metabunk.org/attachments/1792039093196-png.93642/\" alt=\"1792039093196.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"703\" height=\"129\" />\n\t</p><p>\nlasting a duration five minutes and more.(whatever more means in this context?)</p><p><img src=\"https://www.metabunk.org/attachments/1792039324864-png.93643/\" alt=\"1792039324864.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"693\" height=\"125\" />\n\t</p><p>\n\nCommenters proposed:</p><ol>\n<li><b>Hydrothermal vent:</b> Heat and minerals rising from the seabed.</li>\n<li><b>Sewage outfall:</b> Wastewater creating foam and turbulence.</li>\n<li><b>Methane release:</b> Escaping seabed gas producing bubbles.</li>\n<li><b>Sediment eruption:</b> Pressurised water lifting mud or minerals.</li>\n<li><b>Whale feeding:</b> Bottom-feeding stirring up sediment.</li>\n<li><b>Whale waste:</b> Faeces or vomit discolouring the water.</li>\n<li><b>Dead whale:</b> Decomposition releasing gas and fluids.</li>\n<li><b>Submarine:</b> A submerged vessel disturbing the surface.</li>\n<li><b>Feeding frenzy:</b> Predators and baitfish churning the water.</li>\n<li><b>Broken pipeline:</b> Pressurised discharge from a damaged pipe.</li>\n<li><b>Stormwater runoff:</b> Drainage suddenly clouding the water.</li>\n<li><b>Algal bloom:</b> Plankton making the surface appear pale.</li>\n</ol><p>Local reporting in french orginally,<br />\n<a href=\"https://www.lepharillon.info/2026/09/10/pour-63-m-de-projets-daqueduc-et-degouts/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.lepharillon.info/2026/09/10/pour-63-m-de-projets-daqueduc-et-degouts/</a></p><blockquote>\n\t\n\t<p>External Quote:\n\t\t\n\t</p>\n\n\n\t\n\t<p>\n\t\t\tThe Gaspé municipal council adopted three resolutions on September 8 to submit the water and sewer supply projects for Rivière-au-Renard and L'Anse-au-Griffon, for a total value of $63 million.\n\t</p>\n\n</blockquote><p>describes planned water and wastewater infrastructure upgrades in Rivière-au-Renard. That makes checking for an outfall worthwhile, but establishes no cause. </p><p>\n\nI havent looked into any of the claims, nor does this video establish a connection to Nimitz. The comparisons I feel are unavoidable.</p>\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<ul>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t<li>\n\t\t<a></a>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.metabunk.org/data/video/92/92950-32d7636d2f506983eb289fac255d8b2b.mp4?hash=EqLF-fGg1q\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t<p>m2-vp9-res_720p.mp4</p><p>\n\t\t\t\t\t4.8 MB\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\n\t</li>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\n\n\t\t<ul>\n\t\t\t<i></i>\n\t\t\t<i></i>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t<li>\n\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.metabunk.org/threads/what-is-this-white-water-can-it-tied-back-to-nimitz-tic-tac-encounter.15135/post-377385\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t#2\n\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t</ul>\n\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<p>Google earth shows a pipleine heading into the sea off Rivière-au-Renard.</p><p>\n\n48.9958773,-64.3788653. Circle is of radius 500m</p><p><img src=\"https://www.metabunk.org/attachments/1792051344046-png.93644/\" alt=\"1792051344046.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" width=\"1344\" height=\"888\" />\n\t</p><p>\n\n\nPumping station near the shore and pier: <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/place/Rivi%C3%A8re-au-Renard,+QC+G4X+5K7,+Canada/@48.9958773,-64.3788653,7a,77.2y,46.34h,89.44t/data=!3m7!1e1!3m5!1sJT8hoEWyEzLvj5NIty8bSw!2e0!6shttps:%2F%2Fstreetviewpixels-pa.clients6.google.com%2Fv1%2Fthumbnail%3Fcb_client%3Dmaps_sv.tactile%26w%3D900%26h%3D600%26pitch%3D0.55929854666